v 3
d 'DASH': Interactive HTML dashboards from twoway syntax
d
d dash converts Stata twoway plot syntax into interactive dashboards
d powered by the Bokeh visualization library: forty-four twoway plot types,
d multi-graph layouts, linked brushing, filter widgets
d (dropdown/multi/slider/range) and KPI cards.  Most twoway options are
d honoured; the rest are accepted and named in a note -- see
d -help dash-, Unsupported Stata twoway options.
d
d A saved dashboard is one self-contained HTML file, with BokehJS
d embedded, that opens in a modern browser without a server or an
d internet connection.  -dash serve- runs the dashboard on a Bokeh
d Server instead, and -dash build- with the server option writes such
d an app for you to launch.
d
d Requires: Stata 19 or later; tested on StataNow 19.5 (MP), macOS arm64.
d Measured on MP only; Stata 19.0, Stata/BE and Stata/SE have not been run.
d Requires: Python 3.11+, bokeh>=3.8,<3.10, numpy>=2.3, pandas>=2.3.
d
d Run -dash_setup- once after installation: it checks the
d dependencies and installs the missing Python packages; where the
d Python refuses pip installs (PEP 668), -dash_setup, venv(path)-
d sets up a private environment instead.
d
d Version: 0.1.0  18oct2026
d Distribution-Date: 20261018
d Author: Billy Buchanan
d Support: william@williambuchanan.net
d KW: twoway
d KW: dashboard
d KW: bokeh
d KW: interactive graphics
d
